WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.200 --> 00:00:04.604
Your files and passwords, encrypted on your own devices,

2
00:00:04.604 --> 00:00:07.643
and kept in step through storage you already have.

3
00:00:08.093 --> 00:00:09.480
This is SilentSilo.

4
00:00:11.080 --> 00:00:15.069
A silo is an encrypted folder on your computer, with its own keys.

5
00:00:15.519 --> 00:00:21.362
Every change is encrypted on the device that made it, then written to storage you choose:

6
00:00:21.362 --> 00:00:25.695
Google Drive, OneDrive or Dropbox, a NAS, or a server of your own.

7
00:00:26.145 --> 00:00:28.364
Your other devices pick it up from there.

8
00:00:28.814 --> 00:00:34.537
The storage only holds encrypted objects. It sees their sizes and when they changed,

9
00:00:34.537 --> 00:00:37.603
never your file names, contents or passwords.

10
00:00:38.053 --> 00:00:42.234
There is no SilentSilo server in between, and no account to create.

11
00:00:43.834 --> 00:00:47.119
There is no password to remember, or for anyone to guess.

12
00:00:47.569 --> 00:00:51.131
You open a silo with what your devices already have:

13
00:00:51.131 --> 00:00:55.377
Windows Hello, your fingerprint or Face ID, or a security key.

14
00:00:55.827 --> 00:00:59.774
A recovery code on paper is the way back if a device is lost.

15
00:01:01.374 --> 00:01:05.513
Let's set one up on Windows. Give the silo a name and pick a folder.

16
00:01:05.963 --> 00:01:08.715
Choose how it unlocks. Here, Windows Hello.

17
00:01:09.165 --> 00:01:12.216
Next comes the recovery code. It is shown once.

18
00:01:12.666 --> 00:01:17.189
Write it down, or print the emergency kit, and keep it away from the computer.

19
00:01:17.639 --> 00:01:23.271
Then the backup storage. We'll use Google Drive: sign in, and the encrypted copy goes there.

20
00:01:23.721 --> 00:01:25.001
The silo is ready.

21
00:01:26.601 --> 00:01:30.292
Drop in files and folders, and open them with a double-click.

22
00:01:30.742 --> 00:01:35.030
Logins, cards, notes and two-factor codes live under Passwords.

23
00:01:35.480 --> 00:01:39.768
On disk, everything in the silo is encrypted, file names included.

24
00:01:40.218 --> 00:01:44.335
And it locks itself when you lock the computer, or after a while unused.

25
00:01:45.935 --> 00:01:50.383
Now the phone. Install SilentSilo from Google Play or the App Store,

26
00:01:50.383 --> 00:01:52.868
and choose Set up from backup storage.

27
00:01:53.318 --> 00:01:56.219
Connect the same Google Drive and pick your silo.

28
00:01:56.669 --> 00:02:00.258
The first time, the phone is let in with your recovery code,

29
00:02:00.258 --> 00:02:02.770
or with your security key held against it.

30
00:02:03.220 --> 00:02:07.487
Then it makes a key of its own, opened by your fingerprint or Face ID.

31
00:02:07.937 --> 00:02:13.270
From now on, the phone and the computer stay in step. Sync starts as soon as you unlock.

32
00:02:14.870 --> 00:02:18.391
On the phone, SilentSilo can also back up new photos,

33
00:02:18.391 --> 00:02:21.846
videos and contacts, encrypted before they leave it.

34
00:02:22.296 --> 00:02:25.112
And it fills your logins in apps and in the browser.

35
00:02:26.612 --> 00:02:33.119
SilentSilo is free and open source, on Windows, macOS, Linux, Android and iPhone.

36
00:02:33.569 --> 00:02:35.830
Download it at silentsilo.com.
